Speech-to-Text and Text-to-Speech using Whisper

Overview
This project uses OpenAI Whisper for speech-to-text conversion and gTTS for text-to-speech generation. It also evaluates transcription accuracy using Word Error Rate (WER).

Technologies Used
- Python
- OpenAI Whisper
- gTTS
- Jiwer
- FFmpeg
- Google Colab

Methodology
1. Upload an audio file.
2. Convert speech into text using Whisper.
3. Detect the language and measure processing time.
4. Compare the recognized text with the reference transcript.
5. Calculate Word Error Rate (WER) and approximate word accuracy.
6. Generate speech output and evaluate the results.

Evaluation Metrics
- Processing Time: Time taken for speech recognition.
- Word Error Rate (WER): Measures transcription errors.
- Word Accuracy: Approximate accuracy calculated from WER.
- TTS Generation: Checks whether speech output was generated successfully.

Conclusion
This project demonstrates speech recognition, transcription evaluation, and speech generation using deep learning and text-to-speech tools.
